{"id": "r02_renderer", "scores": [5, 6], "best": 6, "final": "needs-lead-review", "issues": ["High-frequency allocations: _pushRenderable creates a new closure (arrow function) for every entity, building, and particle every frame. This triggers massive GC pressure.", "Hot loop allocation: renderPool.slice(0, this.renderCount) creates a new array every frame. Use a pre-allocated array of indices or a custom sort that respects renderCount.", "Frame-rate dependent logic: Zoom interpolation (0.15) and smoke spawning (dt * 2) are not properly normalized. Zoom should use 1 - Math.pow(smoothing, dt).", "Minimap performance: drawMinimap iterates over the entire 96x96 grid every call. This should be cached to an offscreen canvas and only updated when terrain/territory/buildings change.", "Inefficient Territory Borders: _drawTerritoryBorders performs O(N) path operations every frame. These should be cached or drawn to the chunk canvases.", "DPR Inconsistency: tileToScreen/screenToTile divide/multiply by DPR, but the main ctx transform already handles scaling via canvas.width/height setting. This will cause coordinate drift on high-DPI screens.", "String Concatenation: rgba() strings in _drawDayNight and _drawProgressBar are reconstructed every frame. Pre-calculate or use constant color values.", "Missing Robustness: sprites.draw() is called without checking if sprites.has(sName) or if size(sName) exists, which will crash the loop if a single asset is missing."]}
{"id": "u01_ui", "scores": [6], "best": 6, "final": "needs-lead-review", "issues": ["Performance/Architecture: _updateInfoPanel and _updateTooltip overwrite innerHTML every single frame. This causes massive layout thrashing and prevents text selection or sub-element interaction.", "Memory Leak: window.addEventListener('keydown') is never removed. UI needs a destroy() method to clean up global listeners.", "Acceptance Criteria: Using innerHTML to inject game strings (e.g., building names, error reasons) violates the 'no innerHTML with untrusted data' rule. Use textContent for dynamic strings.", "Architecture: _updateStock and _updateObjectives lack dirty-checking. They perform DOM operations every frame/interval regardless of whether the underlying data changed.", "Robustness: JSON.stringify(this.tool) is a slow and brittle way to handle tool state comparison in a hot loop.", "Polish: The 'pixel font' requirement is poorly met; 'Courier New' is a standard monospace font, not a pixel-art font. Use a specific webfont or a more curated stack.", "Logic: The speed button sync in togglePause() is inconsistent with the update() loop. Speed state should have a single source of truth and a reactive update.", "UX: The tooltip for placement problems follows the mouse using raw clientX/Y without accounting for scroll or container offsets, leading to 'jumping' on different resolutions.", "Code Quality: _initDOM is a 'mega-string'. Break into smaller functional components or use a template system to improve maintainability."]}
